Evidentiary: at the cut, no kernel receipt for these 152 declarations exists, either CBZ-indexed or in the group's own directory. MANIFEST.json holds expected axiom lists only. The outputs of gate.py --execute and of the cap-first-exit-lean.yml workflow go to .lake/evidence or a CI artifact, and none is stored or indexed.

Informal alignment: ALIGNMENT §4 keeps four interfaces informal:
- I1: reading P's contact frame and field as φ and the periodic lift;
- I2: identifying the H0 persistence pairing with olderPeakLevels;
- I3: SP §2's setting on G_r;
- I4: the probability side.

ALIGNMENT.md also records where Lean's hypothesis forms differ from SP's, both described as weaker than SP's:
- the ridge_profile row (line 51), and ridge_capHyp's hconv, take convexity of F - q where SP states F'' - 1/4 > 0;
- the ridge_source_facts/ridge_capHyp_C3 row (line 90) takes the third derivatives as derivatives of the scalar maps p ↦ D²f p [a, b].
The principal ridge_capHyp_E and ridge_capHyp_blocks take f ∈ C⁴ through iteratedFDeriv instead.
